{"strongs": "H2975", "word": "יְאֹר", "translit": "ye.or", "root": "יאר", "morph": "N:N--L", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "stream", "definition": "יְאֹר , יְאוֺר noun masculine Exod 7:21 stream of the Nile, stream, canal (Egyptian loan-word = Egyptian °iotr, °io°r , watercourse , Coptic eioor, ior ; also °iotr±o, °io°r±o , Coptic eiero, iaro , Nile , Steind BAs i. 612 ; in Assyrian ia°uru , stream , °Iaru°û , river Nile , Id ib., Hpt ib. 171 Jäger ib 466 ) — absolute הַיְאֹר Gen 41:1 + 37 t.; הַיְאוֺר Isa 19:8 הַיְאֹ֫רָה Exod 1:22 יְאוֺר Isa 19:7 (3 t. in verse) + 2 t.; כָּאֹר (err. for כַּיְאֹר ) Amos 8:8 construct כִּיאֹר Amos 9:5 כִּיאוֺר Amos 8:8 suffix יְאֹרִי Ezek 29:3 b ( Co יאר , compare v Ezek 29:9 and ᵑ6 ᵑ7 ); plural יְאֹרִים Exod 8:1 + 4 t.; construct יְאֹרֵי Isa 7:18 + 2 t.; יְאוֺרֵי 2Kgs 19:24 suffix יְאֹרֶיךָ Ezek 29:4 (twice in verse); Ezek 29:5 + v Ezek 29:4 (strike out ᵐ5 Co ) + Ezek 29:10 ( Co יְאֹרְךָ ); יְאֹרָיו Ezek 29:3 יְאֹדֵיהֶם Exod 7:19 ; Ps 78:44 — 1. stream of the Nile, river Nile , usually with article Gen 41:1 ; Gen 41:2 ; Gen 41:3 (twice in verse); Gen 41:18 ; Exod 1:22 ; Exod 2:3 ; Exod 2:5 (twice in verse); Exod 4:9 (twice in verse); Exod 7:15 ; Exod 7:17 ; Exod 7:18 (3 t. in verse); Exod 7:20 (twice in verse); Exod 7:21 (3 t. in verse); Exod 7:24 (twice in verse); Exod 7:28 ; Exod 8:5 ; Exod 8:7 ; Exod 17:5 (all J E ), Amos 8:8 ; Amos 9:5 ; Isa 19:7 (3 t. in verse); Isa 19:8 ; Isa 23:3 (|| שִׁחֹר ), v Isa 23:10 ; Jer 46:7 ; Jer 46:8 (simile of Egyptian invasion), Ezek 29:3 b (read יאר , see above), v Ezek 29:9 ; Zech 10:11 more fully יְאֹר מִצְרַיִם Amos 8:8 ; Amos 9:5 . 2. plural: \\ \\ a. Nile-arms, Nile-canals , יְאֹרֵי מִצְרַים Isa 7:18 יְאֹרֵי מָצוֺר Isa 19:6 (|| נְהָרוֺת ), Isa 37:25 = 2Kgs 19:24 see also Nah 3:8 ; Exod 7:19 ; Exod 8:1 (both P ; || נְהָרֹת , אֲגַמִּים , etc.), Ps 78:44 (|| נֹזְלִים ), Ezek 29:3 ; Ezek 29:4 (twice in verse); Ezek 29:5 ; Ezek 29:10 + v Ezek 29:4 ᵑ0 (but strike out ᵐ5 Co ), Ezek 30:12 . \\ \\ b. watercourses in general, יְאֹרִים רַחֲבֵי יָדָ֑יִם Isa 33:21 (|| נְהָרִים ; compare Late Hebrew יְאוֺר , late Aramaic יְאוֺרָא ). 3. shafts , made in mining Job 28:10 ( בַּצּוּרוֺת ). 4. יְאֹר , singular, of Tigris , Dan 12:5 (twice in verse); Dan 12:6 ; Dan 12:7 (compare Dan 10:4 ).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3389')\">BDB3389</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H2975')\">H2975</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3388')\">BDB3388</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3390')\">BDB3390</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>יְאֹר</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>יְאוֺר</bdbheb> <b>noun masculine</b><sup><ref ref=\"Exod 7:21\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"21\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"21\" onclick=\"bcv(2,7,21)\">Exod 7:21</ref></sup> <highlightword>stream</highlightword> of the Nile, <highlightword>stream, canal</highlightword> (Egyptian loan-word = Egyptian <transliteration><highlight>°iotr, °io°r</highlight></transliteration>, <highlight>watercourse</highlight>, Coptic <transliteration><highlight>eioor, ior</highlight></transliteration>; also <transliteration><highlight>°iotr±o, °io°r±o</highlight></transliteration>, Coptic <transliteration><highlight>eiero, iaro</highlight></transliteration>, <highlight>Nile</highlight>, <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Steind')\">Steind<sup>BAs i. 612</sup></lookup>; in Assyrian <transliteration><highlight>ia°uru</highlight></transliteration>, <highlight>stream</highlight>, <transliteration><highlight>°Iaru°û</highlight></transliteration>, <highlight>river Nile</highlight>, Id<sup>ib.,</sup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Hpt')\">Hpt<sup>ib. 171</sup></lookup> Jäger<sup>ib 466</sup>) — absolute <bdbheb>הַיְאֹר</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 41:1\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"41\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"41\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(1,41,1)\">Gen 41:1</ref> + 37 t.; <bdbheb>הַיְאוֺר</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 19:8\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(23,19,8)\">Isa 19:8</ref> <bdbheb>הַיְאֹ֫רָ